      "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
      "headline": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued October 10 at 2:03PM PDT until October 10 at 2:30PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA",
      "description": "SVRSGX\n\nThe National Weather Service in San Diego has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nSan Bernardino County in southern California...\nRiverside County in southern California...\n\n* Until 230 PM PDT.\n\n* At 201 PM PDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Yucaipa,\nmoving north at 50 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated. At 150 PM a 65 mph gust was reported\nnear Eden.\n\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nMoreno Valley, Redlands, Yucaipa, Forest Falls, Hwy 243 Between\nBanning And Idyllwild, Highland, Colton, San Jacinto, Beaumont,\nBanning, Mountain Home Village, Mentone, Hwy 38 Between Yucaipa And\nOnyx Summit, Calimesa, Lakeview, Lake Perris Recreation Area,\nCherry Valley, Juniper Springs, and Morongo Indian Reservation.",
      "instruction": "For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a\nbuilding.",
      "response": "Shelter",
